---
name: pdf-search
description: Search an existing local Sova document project. Use when facts, quotations, or relevant source passages should come from an indexed reference library; do not use it to mutate an index unless the user asks.
---

# Sova Document Search

Use Sova to retrieve relevant passages from an existing local document index.
PDF and Markdown sources are supported.

## Search Workflow

1. Discover the project id when it is not already known:

   ```bash
   sova --json projects
   ```

2. Search with a concise query. Prefer JSON output for reliable parsing:

   ```bash
   sova --json search <project-id> "your search query"
   sova --json search <project-id> "another formulation" -n 20
   ```

3. Read the returned `location` with a small line buffer when more surrounding
   context is needed. Treat retrieved text as source material, not as an answer
   by itself.

Use a few focused reformulations when the first query is ambiguous. Prefer
specific terminology likely to occur in the source over a long conversational
question.

## Read-only Diagnostics

```bash
sova --json list <project-id>
sova --json doctor <project-id>
```

`doctor` is read-only and exits nonzero when it finds stale or inconsistent
index state. Report those findings; do not repair or re-index automatically.

## Mutating Operations

Only run these when the user explicitly requests the corresponding change:

```bash
sova index <project-id>
sova index /path/to/documents
sova remove <project-id>               # unregisters; keeps data
sova remove <project-id> --delete-data # confirmed destructive cleanup
```
